<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edvard Beneš</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edvard Beneš was a Czech politician who worked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-garrigue-masaryk">Tomáš Garrigue Masaryk</a> for Czechoslovak independence and served as foreign minister from 1918 to 1935. As president from 1935, he resigned after the Munich Agreement of 1938, led the government in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and returned in 1945. He signed the decrees expelling the Germans and resigned in June 1948 after the communist takeover.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edvard-benes.jpg" alt="Edvard Beneš" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown . Transfer; United States. Office of War Information. Overseas Picture Division. Washington Division; 1944. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edvard_Bene%C5%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
